    "kind": "good",
    "note": "Three steps, two of them proton transfers, and a catalytic cycle that closes. This is the fixture to compare against good-cyanohydrin-formation-from-acetaldehyde: same carbonyl, same kind of nucleophile, opposite order of events. Under acid the carbonyl is protonated before the nucleophile arrives, which is why a weak nucleophile like water can add at all; under neutral or basic conditions a strong nucleophile adds first and the oxygen is protonated afterwards. Getting that order backwards is a distinct wrong answer rather than a sloppy one and deserves its own named cause."
